<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abiy Ahmed</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1976</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abiy Ahmed is an Ethiopian politician who became prime minister in 2018 after years of protests. He made peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a>, ending the long stalemate after the border war, and won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a> in 2019. His government then fought the Tigray war of 2020 to 2022 against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigray-peoples-liberation-front">Tigray People's Liberation Front</a>, a conflict marked by mass atrocities.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abiy-ahmed.jpg" alt="Abiy Ahmed" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ethiopia Prime Minister's Office · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prime_Minister_of_Ethiopia_Abiy_Ahmed_Ali_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
